 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Lessons Learned Survey Template FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a lessons learned survey template?\", \"a\": \"A lessons learned survey template is a reusable set of questions a project team answers after a project closes. It asks what helped and what to change next time, and turns the answers into lessons the next project reads before it starts.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a lessons learned survey template?\", \"a\": \"Describe the project, who should answer, and the phases you want rated to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a>. It builds the survey and a database for every answer. Answer it once yourself, reword any question by prompt, and send it to the team.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions belong in a lessons learned survey template?\", \"a\": \"Beyond the three open questions, give each project phase one 1-5 rating and add one question on whether the project met its goal. Close with a single free-text box for anything the set missed, since the most useful lesson often fits no question.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a lessons learned survey template the same as a training evaluation?\", \"a\": \"No. A lessons learned survey asks a project team what to change on the next project. A training evaluation asks learners whether a course taught them what it promised. For that second job, start from <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/learning-and-development-questions'>learning and development survey questions</a> instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a lessons learned survey template run at each project phase?\", \"a\": \"Yes, and on a project longer than a few months it should. Send a short version at each phase gate that repeats the core questions, then the full survey at close. Lessons from design then reach the build phase while the same people are still on the job.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a lessons learned survey template collect names?\", \"a\": \"Only when the team is large enough to hide behind. On a team of 4 or 5, people can often tell who wrote what, and leaving names off protects little. Say plainly who reads the raw answers. Emergent can build the survey with or without names stored, and a prompt switches it later.\"}, {\"q\": \"What rating scale suits a lessons learned survey template?\", \"a\": \"A 5-point scale from poor to excellent works for rating phases, and keeping the same scale on every project lets you compare them. If you want finer grades on one question, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/slider-scale'>slider scale survey</a> gives a 0-10 range without crowding the screen.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I get more people to fill in a lessons learned survey template?\", \"a\": \"Keep it short, send it from the project sponsor, and open with one change the last survey led to. People answer when they see earlier answers acted on. Set a fixed close date and share a summary of the results within a week of it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one lessons learned survey template compare several projects?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if every project uses identical core questions and one rating scale. Add project-specific questions after the core set, never in place of it. Emergent can build a dashboard that puts two projects' phase scores side by side.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a lessons learned survey template include customer feedback?\", \"a\": \"No. Keep customer feedback in its own survey and bring a summary of its results to the lessons review, where the team reads it next to its own answers. Mixing the two in one form blurs who said what.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 },
